The research's work on wl-cross-domain-proxy (virtio-gpu-desktop,
src/wl-cross-domain-proxy at its commit 8ecffaf), as one diff against
upstream c6ce1ca89fb4, the commit it started from
(patches/wl-cross-domain-proxy/BASE.md there).  What the nested desktop
needs of the proxy beyond upstream: the presentation clock translated into
the guest's, fence waits before a frame reaches the host, the host's pointer
grab and shortcut capture, the clipboard following the window's focus, an
opaque toplevel, resizes settled before they reach the guest, AMD DCC
modifiers left out of the dma-buf feedback (the host can scan the frames out
then), statistics and their overlay, and the host's hang-up: an empty
receive (the host end of the connection closed: the app serving QEMU's
socket quit or crashed) closes that guest client, whose compositor then
sees its connection end, instead of polling on.

Licence: these changes are GPL-2.0-or-later (the research's, the user's
choice of 2026-10-14); Victoria Brekenfeld's proxy stays MIT, with her
notice in LICENSE, and the ChromiumOS part (src/cross_domain) BSD-style:
the tree as a whole is GPL-2.0-or-later AND MIT (its README and Cargo.toml
say so).

